21/23 adversarial assertions   node tests/headless_agent_api.mjs &amp;&amp; python3 tests/score_adversarial.py</pre>
<p>Two of those suites break their own checks on purpose and assert each one goes red (<code>--selftest</code>). A suite that cannot fail proves nothing about the code it passes. The adversarial score is 21 of 23 on purpose: one assertion fails on every run and one alternates, and both are reported rather than averaged away.</p>
